\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces (a) The materialization--completion bottleneck shift and the interior time-to-success optimum at $K^\star {=}8$, measured on the same $35{,}640$-run peer-broadcast sweep (Fig.~\ref {p4:fig:conditional-rates}): $P(M^\star |R^\star )$ falls and $P(C^\star |M^\star )$ rises with $K$, while mean $t_{\mathrm  {succ}}$ has an interior minimum. (b) The measured CSM sweep over cadence $K$ and trust threshold $\tau $: mean $t_{\mathrm  {succ}}$ is essentially $\tau $-invariant and only weakly $K$-dependent, and mission success is flat in $(K,\tau )$ (range $0.015$). The trust threshold is \emph  {not} the active lever in this regime --- the interior operating point is the cadence effect of panel (a), not a two-dimensional optimum island.}}{70}{figure.22}\protected@file@percent }
